From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:11:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let a theme style and place the info popups and the meters

The info popups (a notice sent through the API, a song's title) were
drawn in the menu's frame and font at the top centre, one under the
other with no limit, over whatever the theme draws there; the volume
and brightness meters were vertical bars in the top left corner with
no sign of which one changed and a track and fill of nearly the same
colour.

With a size, the screen view's notification element named
"notification" places the popups (pos, origin, spacing) and draws
them as a box of the theme's (font, colours, border, corner radius,
an icon) with the text on one line; maxCount caps those shown at
once, the next one showing when one ends. One named "meters" draws
each meter as a pill with its glyph (a speaker or a sun), a
horizontal bar in the theme's track and fill colours and the level,
side by side when both show. Both are drawn over the screen's extras.
Without these elements nothing changes.
